hadiths[138]{hadithnumber,text}:
"399","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, Yazid, meaning al-Farisi, narrated to us, my father Ahmad ibn Hanbal said, and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Yazid, he said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said to us: I said to Uthman ibn Affan: What carried you to go to al-Anfal, which is from the mathani, and to Baraa, which is from the miin, and join them together, and you did not write, Ibn Jafar said: Between them a line, In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful, and you placed them among the seven long ones, what carried you to that. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, time would pass upon him with suras of number revealed to him, and when something was revealed to him he would call some of those who wrote with him and say: Put this in the sura in which such and such is mentioned. Verses would be revealed to him and he would say: Put these verses in the sura in which such and such is mentioned. A verse would be revealed to him and he would say: Put this verse in the sura in which such and such is mentioned. Al-Anfal was among the first revealed at Medina, and Baraa among the last of the Quran, and its story was like its story. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died without clarifying to us that it was from it. I thought it was from it, so I joined them together, and did not write between them a line, In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful. Ibn Jafar said: And I placed it among the seven long ones."
"400","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, my father informed me that Humran informed him, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, performed wudu on al-Balat, then said: I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah I would not narrate it to you. I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever performs wudu and performs wudu well, then enters and prays, he is forgiven what is between him and the next prayer until he prays it."
"401","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Malik, Nafi' narrated to me from Nubayh ibn Wahb from Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A muhrim does not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"402","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Harmalah, he said: I heard Sa'id, meaning Ibn al-Musayyab, say: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, set out performing Hajj until when he was on part of the road, it was said to Ali, may Allah's pleasure be upon them both, that he had forbidden tamattu' of Umrah with Hajj. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to his companions: When he departs, then depart. Ali and his companions entered ihram for Umrah, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, did not speak to him about that. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Was I not informed that you forbade tamattu' with Umrah. He said: He said: Yes. He said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform tamattu'. He said: Yes."
"403","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il from Amir ibn Shaqiq from Abu Wa'il from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wudu three times three times."
"404","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Nadr from Abu Anas that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, performed wudu at al-Maqa'id three times three times, and with him were men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Is it not thus that you saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform wudu. They said: Yes."
"405","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of you is he who learns the Quran and teaches it."
"406","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Jami' ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever completes wudu as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him, then the prescribed prayers are expiations for what is between them."
"407","Waki' narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Qays said, and Abu Sahlah narrated to me that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said on the Day of the House when he was besieged: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted to me a covenant, and I am patient over it. Qays said: And they used to regard it as that day."
"408","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq, they both said: Sufyan narrated to us from Uthman ibn Hakim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, Abd al-Razzaq said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever prays the Isha and Fajr prayers in congregation, then he is as one who stood a night in prayer. And Abd al-Rahman said: Whoever prays Isha in congregation, then he is as one who stood half a night, and whoever prays Fajr in congregation, then he is as one who stood a night."
"409","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays Isha in congregation, then he is as one who stood half the night, and whoever prays Fajr in congregation, then he is as one who stood the whole night."
"410","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, Ata ibn Farrukh, freedman of the Qurashis, narrated to me that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, bought land from a man, then he was slow with him, then he met him and said to him: What prevented you from taking your wealth. He said: You overpriced me, and I meet no one among the people but he blames me. He said: Does that prevent you. He said: Yes. He said: Then choose between your land and your wealth. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, admitted to Paradise a man who was easy as buyer and seller and judger and claimant."
"411","Isma'il narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Abu Ma'shar from Ibrahim from Alqamah, he said: I was with Ibn Mas'ud while he was with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: What remains for women of you. He said: When women were mentioned, Ibn Mas'ud said: Come near, O Alqamah. He said: And I was a young man. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to young men of the Muhajirun and said: Whoever among you has means, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts more, and whoever does not, then fasting is a shield for him."
"412","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Alqamah ibn Marthad narrating from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The best of you is he who taught the Quran or learned it. Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said: Then Abu Abd al-Rahman said: That is what made me sit in this seat. Hajjaj said: Shu'bah said: Abu Abd al-Rahman did not hear from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, nor from Abdullah, but he heard from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. My father said: And Bahz said: From Shu'bah, Alqamah ibn Marthad informed me, and he said: The best of you is he who learned the Quran and taught it."
"413","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Marthad informed me, and he said in it: He who learned the Quran or taught it."
"414","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj narrated to us, they both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard a man narrating from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There was a man who was easy as seller and buyer and judger and claimant, then he entered Paradise."
"415","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah from Muslim ibn Yasar from Humran ibn Aban from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he called for water and performed wudu, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then washed his face three times and his forearms three times three times, and wiped his head and the backs of his feet, then he laughed and said to his companions: Will you not ask me what made me laugh. They said: What made you laugh, O Commander of the Believers. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, call for water near this spot and perform wudu as I performed wudu, then he laughed and said: Will you not ask me what made me laugh. They said: What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When a servant calls for wudu and washes his face, Allah removes from him every sin he committed with his face, and when he washes his forearms it is likewise, and when he wipes his head it is likewise, and when he purifies his feet it is likewise."
"416","Bahz narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, freedman of Hasan ibn Ali, from Rabah, he said: My family married me to a Roman slave girl of theirs, and I had intercourse with her, and she bore me a black boy like me, and I named him Abdullah. Then I had intercourse with her, and she bore me a black boy like me, and I named him Ubaydullah. Then a Roman boy belonging to my family, called Yuhannas, inclined toward her and spoke to her in her tongue. He said: She bore a boy as if a gecko among geckos. I said to her: What is this. She said: He is Yuhannas's. He said: We were raised to the Commander of the Believers, Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him. Mahdi said: I think he said: He asked them both and they confessed. He said: Are you both pleased that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged that the child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone. Mahdi said: And I think he said: He lashed her and lashed him, and they were both slaves."
"417","Shayban Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd from Rabah, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: I raised them both to the Commander of the Believers, Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged that the child belongs to the bed, and he mentioned the like of it."
"418","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Ata ibn Yazid from Humran, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, called for water while he was at al-Maqa'id, and poured over his right hand and washed it, then put his right hand into the vessel and washed his hands three times, then washed his face three times, and rinsed his mouth and blew his nose, and washed his forearms to the elbows three times, then wiped his head, then washed his feet to the ankles three times, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then prays two rak'ahs in which he does not talk to himself, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"419","Ibrahim ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Ata ibn Yazid from Humran, freedman of Uthman, that he saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, call for a vessel, and he mentioned the like of it."
"420","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us from his father from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, looked out from the palace while he was besieged and said: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Hira when the mountain shook and he kicked it with his foot then said: Be still, Hira, there is upon you none but a prophet or a truthful one or a martyr, and I was with him, then men testified for him. He said: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Bay'at al-Ridwan when he sent me to the polytheists, to the people of Makkah, he said: This is my hand and this is the hand of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, then he pledged for me, then men testified for him. He said: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Who will expand for us this house in the mosque with a house in Paradise, then I bought it with my wealth and expanded the mosque with it, then men testified for him. He said: And I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the army of hardship, he said: Who will spend today an accepted expenditure, then I equipped half the army with my wealth. He said: Then men testified for him. And I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed Rumah whose water was sold to the traveler, then I bought it with my wealth and made it free for the traveler. He said: Then men testified for him."
"421","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Humran ibn Aban, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, perform wudu: he poured over his hands three times and washed them, then rinsed his mouth and blew his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then the left likewise, then wiped his head, then washed his right foot three times, then the left likewise. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform wudu similar to this wudu of mine, then he said: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then prays two rak'ahs in which he does not talk to himself, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"422","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Ayyub from Nafi' from Nubayh ibn Wahb, he said: Umar ibn Ubaydullah sent to Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him: Should he apply kohl to his eyes while he is a muhrim, or with what should he apply kohl to them while muhrim. He sent to him that he should bandage them both with aloes, for I heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrate that from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"423","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Ubayd from Humran ibn Aban from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever knows that prayer is a true obligation enters Paradise."
"424","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar, meaning al-Bara, whose name is Yusuf ibn Yazid, narrated to me, Ibn Harmalah narrated to us from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Uthman performed Hajj until when he was on part of the road, Ali was informed that Uthman forbade his companions tamattu' of Umrah with Hajj. Ali said to his companions: When he departs at noon, then depart. Ali and his companions entered ihram for Umrah, and Uthman did not speak to them. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Was I not informed that you forbade tamattu'. Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not perform tamattu'. He said: I do not know what Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, answered him."
"425","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to me, and while I was thus, his freedman Yarfa came to him and said: Here are Uthman and Abd al-Rahman and Sa'd and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. He said: I do not know whether he mentioned Talhah or not, seeking permission to enter upon you. He said: Permit them. Then he remained a while, then he came and said: Here are al-Abbas and Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, seeking permission to enter upon you. He said: Permit them both. When al-Abbas entered, he said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between me and this one, and at that time they were disputing about what Allah granted His Messenger of the wealth of Banu al-Nadir. The people said: Judge between them, O Commander of the Believers, and relieve each one of his fellow, for their dispute has lasted long. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I adjure you by Allah by Whose permission the heavens and earth stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited, what we leave is charity. They said: He said that. And he said to them both the like of that, and they both said: Yes. He said: I shall inform you about this fay. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, singled out His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from it with something He did not give another. He said: And what Allah granted His Messenger from them, you did not spur over it any horses nor camels, and it belonged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, specially. By Allah, he did not withhold it from you nor prefer himself with it over you. He divided it among you and spread it among you until there remained of it this wealth. He used to spend on his family from it for a year, then make what remained of it as Allah's wealth. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am the guardian of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after him; I act in it as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to act in it."
"426","Abdullah narrated to us, Isma'il Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah from Aban ibn Uthman from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw a funeral and stood for it, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, see a funeral and stand for it."
"427","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from Abu Ubayd, he said: I witnessed Ali and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the day of al-Fitr and al-Nahr praying then turning away and reminding the people, and I heard them both say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fasting these two days."
"428","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Ata ibn Yazid al-Junda'i that he heard Humran, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I saw the Commander of the Believers, Uthman, perform wudu: he poured over his hands three times, then blew his nose three times and rinsed his mouth three times, and he mentioned the hadith with the like of the meaning of Ma'mar's hadith."
"429","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us from Urwah ibn Qabisah from a man of the Ansar from his father that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not show you how the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was. They said: Yes. He called for water and rinsed his mouth three times and blew his nose three times, and washed his face and his forearms three times, and wiped his head, and washed his feet three times, then he said: And know that the ears are from the head. Then he said: I have aimed for you the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"430","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Awf al-A'rabi narrated to us from Ma'bad al-Juhani from Humran ibn Aban, he said: We were with Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he called for water and performed wudu. When he finished his wudu, he smiled and said: Do you know what I laughed from. He said: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wudu as I performed wudu, then he smiled, then he said: Do you know what I laughed from. He said: We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: When a servant performs wudu and completes his wudu, then enters his prayer and completes his prayer, he exits his prayer as he exited his mother's belly of sins."
"431","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Shaqiq say: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, used to forbid mut'ah, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to give fatwa with it. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said a word to him, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: You knew that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Yes, but we were afraid. Shu'bah said: I said to Qatadah: What was their fear. He said: I do not know."
"432","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Qatadah, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, used to forbid mut'ah, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to command it. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said a word to Ali, then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You knew that we performed tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes, but we were afraid."
"433","Rawh narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us from Mus'ab ibn Thabit from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said while addressing on his pulpit: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; nothing prevented me from narrating it to you except miserliness toward you. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Guarding a night in the path of Allah, the Exalted, is better than a thousand nights whose night is stood in prayer and whose day is fasted."
"434","Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Ja'far, narrated to us from his father from Mahmud ibn Labid from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Allah builds for him the like of it in Paradise."
"435","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, he said: I saw Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Uthman praying on the day of al-Fitr and al-Adha, then turning away and reminding the people. He said: And I heard them both say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fasting these two days. He said: And I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that anything of your sacrifices remain with you after three."
"436","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, he said: I entered upon Ibn Darah, freedman of Uthman. He said: He heard me rinsing my mouth. He said: He said: O Muhammad. He said: I said: At your service. He said: Shall I not inform you of the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was at al-Maqa'id, call for wudu and rinse his mouth three times and sniff water three times, and wash his face three times and his forearms three times, and wipe his head three times, and wash his feet, then he said: Whoever loves to look at the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then this is the wudu of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"437","Sulayman ibn Harb and Affan, with the same meaning, narrated to us, they both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: We were with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was besieged in the house, and he entered an entrance which, when he entered it, whoever was on the Balat heard his speech. He said: He entered that entrance and came out to us and said: They are threatening me with killing just now. He said: We said: Allah suffices you against them, O Commander of the Believers. He said: And for what would they kill me. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieved after his Islam, or committed adultery after his ihsan, or killed a soul, so he is killed for it. By Allah, I have never loved to have a substitute for my religion since Allah guided me, nor did I commit adultery in Jahiliyyah nor in Islam ever, nor did I kill a soul, so for what would they kill me."
"438","Abdullah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to us, he said: I was with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, in the house while he was besieged, and he said: We used to enter an entrance, and he mentioned the hadith the like of it, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, and he mentioned the hadith the like of it or similar to it."
"439","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, called people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them Ammar ibn Yasir, and said: I shall ask you, and I love that you tell me truthfully. I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to favor Quraysh over all people, and favor Banu Hashim over all Quraysh. The people fell silent. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If the keys of Paradise were in my hand, I would give them to Banu Umayyah until they enter from the last of them. He sent to Talhah and al-Zubayr, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Shall I not narrate to you both about him, meaning Ammar. I came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, holding my hand, walking in al-Batha, until he came upon his father and his mother and Ali being tortured. The father of Ammar said: O Messenger of Allah, forever thus. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Be patient. Then he said: O Allah, forgive the family of Yasir, and I have done."
"440","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hurayth ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Humran narrated to me from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Everything besides the shade of a house, and a crust of bread, and a garment covering his private parts, and water, then what exceeds this, the son of Adam has no right in it."
"441","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us from an elder of Thaqif whom Humayd described with righteousness, he mentioned that his uncle informed him that he saw Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, sit at the second door of the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and call for a shoulder and eat its meat, then stand and pray without performing wudu. Then he said: I sat in the seat of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ate what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate, and did what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did."
"442","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to us from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman, that he narrated to him, he said: I heard Uthman at Mina say: O people, I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he says: Ribat of a day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other than it, so let a man perform ribat as he wishes. Have I conveyed. They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness."
"443","Abu Sa'id, meaning freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Bahili narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us from his father that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed at Mina four rak'ahs, and the people objected to him. He said: O people, I married in Makkah since I arrived, and I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever marries in a land, let him pray the prayer of a resident."
"444","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Musa ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, addressing on the pulpit, saying: I used to buy dates from a clan of the Jews called Banu Qaynuqa and sell them for profit. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Uthman, when you buy, take full measure, and when you sell, give measure."
"445","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Musa ibn Wardan narrated to us from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"446","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father from Aban ibn Uthman from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah with Whose name nothing harms in the earth nor in the heaven, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing, nothing harms him."
"447","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah from Muslim ibn Yasar from Humran ibn Aban that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I know a word none says truthfully from his heart but he is forbidden to the Fire. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: I shall narrate to you what it is. It is the word of sincerity by which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, honored Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions, and it is the word of piety which the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pressed upon his uncle Abu Talib at death: testimony that there is no god but Allah."
"448","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Husayn, meaning al-Mu'allim, narrated to us from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salamah informed me that Ata ibn Yasar informed him that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani informed him that he asked Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him: I said: What do you think if he has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate. Uthman said: He performs wudu as he performs wudu for prayer and washes his penis. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I asked about that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Talhah ibn Ubaydullah and Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and they ordered him with that."
"449","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas say: We raise in degrees whom We will, he said: By knowledge. I said: Who narrated to you. He said: Zayd ibn Aslam claimed that."
"450","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Masarrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I prayed and did not know whether I prayed even or odd. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware of Satan playing with you in your prayers. Whoever of you prays and does not know whether he prayed even or odd, let him prostrate two prostrations, for they complete his prayer."
"451","Yahya ibn Ma'in and Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, they both said: Sawwar Abu Umarah al-Ramli narrated to us from Masirrah ibn Ma'bad, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah led us in Asr prayer and turned to us after his prayer and said: I prayed with Marwan ibn al-Hakam and he prostrated the like of these two prostrations, then he turned to us and informed us that he prayed with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it, similar to it."
"452","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Mughirah ibn Muslim Abu Salamah mention from Matar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, looked out upon his companions while he was besieged and said: For what do you kill me. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who commits adultery after his ihsan, upon him is stoning, or kills intentionally, upon him is retaliation, or apostatizes after his Islam, upon him is killing. By Allah, I never committed adultery in Jahiliyyah nor Islam, nor did I kill anyone so I offer myself in retaliation from him, nor did I apostatize since I embraced Islam. I testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"453","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Abdullah al-Bardadi narrating from Abu Dharr that he came seeking permission upon Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he permitted him, with his staff in his hand. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Ka'b, Abd al-Rahman died and left wealth, what do you think about it. He said: If he paid in it Allah's right, then there is no harm upon him. Abu Dharr raised his staff and struck Ka'b and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I would not love that this mountain were gold for me, I spend it and it is accepted from me, that I leave behind of it six ounces. I adjure you by Allah, O Uthman, did you hear it, three times. He said: Yes."
"454","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir al-Qass narrated to me from Hani, freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, when he stood upon a grave, wept until he wet his beard. It was said to him: You remember Paradise and Hell and do not weep, and you weep from this. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The grave is the first station of the Hereafter; if one is saved from it, then what is after it is easier than it, and if one is not saved from it, then what is after it is harder than it. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, I never saw a sight at all but the grave is more terrible than it."
"455","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Marwan, and I do not think him accused against us, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, suffered a nosebleed in the year of nosebleed until he stayed back from Hajj and made a will. A man of Quraysh entered upon him and said: Appoint a successor. He said: And they said it. He said: Yes. He said: Who is he. He said: He fell silent. He said: Then another man entered upon him and said to him the like of what the first said to him, and he answered him similarly. He said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Did they say al-Zubayr. He said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he was the best of them as I knew and the most beloved of them to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"456","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd narrated it to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us with its isnad the like of it."
"457","Zakariyya ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah, he said: Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a funeral and stood for it, and said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a funeral and stood for it, then he narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a funeral and stood for it."
"458","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah that Ata ibn Yasar informed him from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he informed him that he asked Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him: He said: I said: What do you think if a man has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: He performs wudu as he performs wudu for prayer and washes his penis. He said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I asked about that Ali ibn Abi Talib and al-Zubayr and Talhah and Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and they ordered him with that."
"459","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Yahya from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, he said: Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Humran ibn Aban informed him, he said: I came to Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was sitting at al-Maqa'id, and he performed wudu and performed wudu well. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in this seat, perform wudu and perform wudu well, then he said: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then comes the mosque and bows in it two rak'ahs, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin. And he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And do not be deceived."
"460","Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Umar al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: I heard my uncle Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Musa say: I was with Sulayman ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and an elder of Quraysh entered. Sulayman said: Look at the elder and seat him in a good seat, for Quraysh has a right. I said: O commander, shall I not narrate to you a hadith that reached me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes. He said: I said to him: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever insults Quraysh, Allah insults him. He said: Glory be to Allah, how good this is. Who narrated this to you. He said: I said: Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated it to me from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My father said to me: O my son, if you govern anything of people's affairs, honor Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever insults Quraysh, Allah insults him."
"461","Isma'il ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah from Ibn Abza from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said to him when he was besieged: I have excellent camels I prepared for you, will you move to Makkah, then whoever wishes to come to you will come to you. He said: No, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A ram of Quraysh desecrates Makkah; his name is Abdullah; upon him is like half the sins of people."
"462","Abdullah ibn Bakr and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, they both said: Sa'id narrated to us from Matar and Ya'la ibn Hakim from Nafi' from Nubayh ibn Wahb from Aban ibn Uthman ibn Affan from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A muhrim does not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"463","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said while addressing on his pulpit: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; nothing prevented me from narrating it to you except miserliness with you. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Guarding a night in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights whose night is stood in prayer and whose day is fasted."
"464","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid from Abu Bishr al-Anbari from Humran ibn Aban from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever dies while he knows that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"465","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, Nubayh ibn Wahb narrated to me that Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ma'mar, his eye became inflamed while he was a muhrim, and he wanted to apply kohl to it, and Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, forbade him and ordered him to bandage it with aloes, and claimed that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he did that."
"466","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us from Nubayh ibn Wahb that Umar ibn Ubaydullah wanted to marry his son while he was a muhrim, and Aban forbade him, and claimed that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A muhrim does not marry, nor give in marriage."
"467","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrating from Rabah, he said: My family married me to a Roman slave girl of theirs who bore me a black boy, then a Roman slave called Yuhannas coveted her and spoke to her in Latin, and she became pregnant, though she had borne me a black boy like me, and she brought a boy as if a gecko among geckos. I said to her: What is this. She said: He is from Yuhannas. I asked Yuhannas and he confessed. I came to Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and mentioned that to him. He sent to them both and asked them both, then he said: I shall judge between you both by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The child belongs to the bed, and for the fornicator is the stone. He attached him to me. He said: He lashed them both, and she later bore me a black boy."
"468","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: I was with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, in the house while he was besieged. He said: We used to enter an entrance which, when we entered it, we heard the speech of whoever was on the Balat. He said: Uthman entered one day for a need and came out to us with his color changed. He said: They are threatening me with killing just now. He said: We said: Allah suffices you against them, O Commander of the Believers. He said: For what would they kill me. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except in one of three: a man who disbelieved after his Islam, or committed adultery after his ihsan, or killed a soul without a soul. By Allah, I never committed adultery in Jahiliyyah nor Islam, nor did I wish a substitute for my religion since Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guided me, nor did I kill a soul, so for what would they kill me."
"469","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, and Surayj and Husayn, they both said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father from Amir ibn Sa'd, Husayn said: Ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Nothing prevents me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I am not the most retentive of his companions from him, but I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. Husayn said: The most retentive of his companions from him."
"470","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad al-Qurashi narrated to me from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, say on the pulpit: O people, I concealed from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, out of dislike that you scatter from me, then it occurred to me to narrate it to you so a man may choose for himself what occurs to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Ribat of a day in the path of Allah, the Exalted, is better than a thousand days in other stations."
"471","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from Salih ibn Kaysan from a man from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim leaves his house intending travel or other than it, and says when he leaves: In the name of Allah, I believed in Allah, I held to Allah, I relied upon Allah, there is no power nor strength except by Allah, but he is granted the good of that exit and the evil of that exit is averted from him."
"472","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Ata from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform wudu: he washed his face three times and his hands three times, and wiped his head, and washed his feet with washing."
"473","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhrah Jami' ibn Shaddad informed me, he said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating to Abu Burdah in the mosque of Basra, while I was standing with him, that he heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever completes wudu as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him, then the five prayers are expiation for what is between them."
"474","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says at the start of his day or at the start of his night: In the name of Allah with Whose name nothing harms in the earth nor in the heaven, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing, three times, nothing harms him in that day or in that night."
"475","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu Sinan informed us from Yazid ibn Mawhab that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Judge between people. He said: I do not judge between two, nor lead two. Did you not hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever seeks refuge with Allah has sought a great refuge. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Yes. He said: I seek refuge with Allah that you employ me. He excused him and said: Do not inform anyone of this."
"476","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Uthman ibn Hakim, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us from Humran from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever performs wudu and performs wudu well, his sins exit his body until they exit from under his nails."
"477","Abdullah narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated it to us in the year two hundred and twenty-six, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that Uthman said: O people, come early, for I am coming early. The people came early. Then he said: O people, I shall narrate to you a hadith I did not speak of since I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until this day of mine. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ribat of a day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days of other than it, so let a man perform ribat where he wishes. Have I conveyed to you. They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness."
"478","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, Shaqiq ibn Salamah narrated to me from Humran, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was sitting at al-Maqa'id and called for wudu and performed wudu, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform wudu in this seat of mine, then he said: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then stands and bows two rak'ahs, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not be deceived."
"479","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Artah, meaning Ibn al-Mundhir, narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ansari informed me that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Mas'ud: Will you stop what reached me about you. He offered some excuse. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Woe to you, I heard and memorized, and it is not as you heard: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A commander will be killed, and a usurper will rise, and I am the one killed, and it is not Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Only one killed Umar, and they gather against me."
"480","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, my father narrated to me from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar informed him that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O son of my brother, did you meet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said to him: No, but there reached me of his knowledge and certainty what reaches the virgin in her veil. He said: He testified, then he said: As for after, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the truth, and I was among those who responded to Allah and His Messenger and believed in what Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sent with. Then I migrated the two migrations as you said, and attained marriage kinship to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. By Allah, I neither disobeyed him nor deceived him until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."
"481","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: And al-Awza'i informed me from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he narrated to him from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah that he entered upon Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was besieged, and said: You are the imam of the public, and what you see has befallen you, and I offer you three options; choose one of them: either you go out and fight them, for with you are numbers and strength, and you are upon truth and they are upon falsehood; or we make for you a door other than the door they are at, then you sit upon your mounts and join Makkah, for they will not violate you while you are in it; or you join Sham, for they are the people of Sham and among them is Mu'awiyah. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for going out to fight, I shall never be the first who succeeded the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his nation by shedding blood. As for going out to Makkah, they will not violate me in it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A man of Quraysh desecrates Makkah; upon him is half the punishment of the world, and I shall never be him. As for joining Sham, they are the people of Sham and among them is Mu'awiyah, then I shall never leave my house of migration and neighborhood of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"482","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated it to us from Ibn al-Mubarak, and he mentioned the hadith and said: Desecrates."
"483","Hajjaj and Yunus narrated to us, they both said: Layth narrated to us, Hajjaj said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah and Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi from Humran, freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from Uthman that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever performs wudu and completes wudu, then walks to a prescribed prayer and prays it, his sin is forgiven."
"484","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Asim from al-Musayyab from Musa ibn Talhah from Humran, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, used to bathe every day once since he embraced Islam. I placed wudu for him one day for prayer. When he performed wudu, he said: I intended to narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then it occurred to me not to narrate it to you. Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As said: O Commander of the Believers, if it is good we take it, or evil we avoid it. He said: He said: I shall narrate it to you: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wudu this wudu, then he said: Whoever performs wudu this wudu and performs wudu well, then stands to prayer and completes its bowing and prostration, it expiates for him what is between it and the next prayer, so long as he does not commit a mortal sin, meaning a major sin."
"485","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Yunus from Ata ibn Farrukh from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah admitted to Paradise a man who was easy as judger and claimant and seller and buyer."
"486","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, a man of the people of Madinah narrated to me that the muezzin called for Asr prayer. He said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, called for purification and purified himself. He said: Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever purifies himself as commanded and prays as commanded, his sins are expiated for him. He called to witness over that four of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: They bore witness for him to that upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"487","Ibn al-Ashja'i narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Sufyan from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Busr ibn Sa'id, he said: Uthman came to al-Maqa'id and called for wudu, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then washed his face three times and his hands three times three times, then wiped his head and his feet three times three times, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, thus perform wudu. O people, is it thus. They said: Yes, to a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with him."
"488","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to me from Busr ibn Sa'id from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he called for water and performed wudu at al-Maqa'id, and performed wudu three times three times, then he said to the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did you see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do this. They said: Yes. My father said: This al-Adani was in Makkah, the scribe of Ibn Uyaynah."
"489","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me from Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi from Humran ibn Aban, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, call for wudu while he was at the door of the mosque, and wash his hands, then rinse his mouth and sniff water and blow his nose, then wash his face three times, then wash his hands to the elbows three times, then wipe his head and pass his hands over the outer ears, then pass them both over his beard, then wash his feet to the ankles three times, then stand and bow two rak'ahs, then he said: I performed wudu for you as I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform wudu, then I bowed two rak'ahs as I saw him bow. He said: Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said when he finished his two rak'ahs: Whoever performs wudu as I performed wudu, then bows two rak'ahs in which he does not talk to himself, he is forgiven what was between them and his prayer yesterday."
"490","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us from Asim from Shaqiq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf met al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and al-Walid said to him: Why do I see you have estranged the Commander of the Believers, Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd al-Rahman said to him: Convey to him that I did not flee on the day of Aynayn, Asim says: meaning the day of Uhud, nor was I absent on the day of Badr, nor did I abandon the sunna of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: He went and informed Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, of that. He said: He said: As for his saying I did not flee on the day of Aynayn, how does he reproach me for a sin Allah forgave, for He said: Those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met, Satan only caused them to slip for some of what they earned, and Allah forgave them. As for his saying I was absent on the day of Badr, I was nursing Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when she died, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck my share for me, and whoever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck his share for has witnessed. As for his saying I did not abandon the sunna of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, I cannot bear it, nor he, so go and narrate that to him."
"491","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Sahl, meaning Uthman ibn Hakim, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays Isha in congregation, it is as standing half a night, and whoever prays Isha and Fajr in congregation, it is as standing a night."
"492","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Nafi' from Nubayh ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Ma'mar wanted to marry his son to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr, so he sent me to Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was the amir of the Hajj season. I came to him and said to him: Your brother wanted to marry his son, and wanted you to witness that. He said: Do I not see him an uncouth Iraqi. A muhrim does not marry, nor give in marriage. Then he narrated from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, the like of it, raising it."
"493","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Hisham from his father from Humran, freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that Uthman performed wudu at al-Maqa'id and washed three times three times, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then stands to prayer, his sins fall, meaning from his face and his hands and his feet and his head."
"494","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Nubayh ibn Wahb, he said: Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ma'mar complained of his eyes, and sent to Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, Sufyan said: While he was amir, what should he do with them. He said: He said: Bandage them both with aloes, for I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, narrate that from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"495","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa Abu Salih narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah from Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw an approaching funeral, and when he saw it, he stood, and said: I saw Uthman do that, and he informed me that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do it."
"496","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Nubayh ibn Wahb from Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from Uthman, conveying to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A muhrim does not marry, nor propose."
"497","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa ibn Amr ibn Sa'id from Nubayh ibn Wahb, a man of al-Hajabah, from Aban ibn Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrated from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave concession, or he said, for a muhrim when his eye complains to bandage it with aloes."
"498","Isma'il narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from al-Walid Abu Bishr from Humran from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever dies while he knows that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"499","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to us, Yazid al-Farisi narrated to me, Ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: I said to Uthman: What prompted you to turn to Surah al-Anfal, which is of the Mathani, and to Surah Bara'ah, which is of the Mi'in, then join them and not write between them the line: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and place them in the Seven Long. What prompted you to that. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when time passed over him while chapters of number were revealed to him, when something was revealed to him, he called one who wrote for him and said: Place these in the surah in which such and such is mentioned. When verses were revealed to him, he said: Place these verses in the surah in which such and such is mentioned. When a verse was revealed to him, he said: Place this verse in the surah in which such and such is mentioned. Surah al-Anfal was among the earliest revealed in Madinah, and Surah Bara'ah was among the last revealed of the Quran. He said: Its story was similar to its story, so we thought it was from it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died and did not clarify to us that it was from it. For that reason I joined them and did not write between them the line: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and placed them in the Seven Long."
"500","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Sufyan and Shu'bah from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Sufyan said: The best of you, and Shu'bah said: The best of you is he who learned the Quran and taught it."
"501","Waki narrated to us from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid who said Qays said: Abu Sahlah narrated to me that Uthman said on the Day of the House when he was besieged: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me a covenant, so I am patient upon it. Qays said: And they used to consider that to be that day."
"502","Yazid narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub from al-Hasan ibn Sad who said: Rabah narrated to me who said: My master married me to a Roman slave girl, so I had intercourse with her and she bore me a black boy like me, so I named him Abdullah. Then I had intercourse with her and she bore me a black boy like me, so I named him Ubaydullah. Then a Roman boy took a liking to me - I think he said to my family - a Roman called Yuhannes, so he spoke to her in his tongue, meaning in Roman, then he had intercourse with her and she bore him a red boy as if he were a gecko. So I said to her: What is this? She said: This is from Yuhannes. He said: So we took our dispute to Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and they both acknowledged. Uthman said: If you wish I will judge between you by the judgement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed. I think he said: And he flogged them both."
"503","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Jami ibn Shaddad who said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating to Abu Burdah in the mosque that he heard Uthman ibn Affan narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever perfects ablution as Allah commanded him, then the prescribed prayers are expiations for what is between them."
"504","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb who said: I heard Abbad ibn Zahir Abu Ruwa who said: I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, addressing, and he said: By Allah, we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in travel and residence, and he used to visit our sick and follow our funerals and raid with us and console us with little and much, and there are people informing me about him, perhaps one of them never saw him at all."
"505","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Shuayb Abu Shaybah narrated to me who said: I heard Ata al-Khurasani saying: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab saying: I saw Uthman sitting in the sitting places, so he called for food touched by fire and ate it, then stood for prayer and prayed, then Uthman said: I sat in the sitting place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and ate the food of the Messenger of Allah, and prayed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"506","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Abdulhamid ibn Jafar narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Mahmud ibn Labid that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, wanted to build the mosque of Madinah, so the people disliked that and loved to leave it as it was, so Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise like it."
"507","Abdul Kabir ibn Abdulmajid Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: Abdulhamid ibn Jafar narrated to us from his father from Mahmud ibn Labid from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies upon me, let him take a house in the Fire."
"508","Ismail narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us: Ata ibn Farrukh, freedman of the Qurashis, narrated to us from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah admitted a man into Paradise who was easy when buying and selling and judging and seeking repayment."
"509","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf who said: We were with Uthman while he was besieged in the house. He said: Why do you kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after chastity, or kills a soul, so he is killed for it."
"510","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Said ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abdurrahman ibn Azhar, who said: I saw Ali and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, praying on the day of Fitr and Adha, then leaving and reminding the people. He said: And I heard them both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days. He said: And I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anything of your sacrifices remain with you after three."
"511","Bahz narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us from Amr ibn Jawan who said: Al-Ahnaf said: We set out as pilgrims and passed by Madinah, and while we were in our lodging a comer came to us and said: The people are in panic in the mosque. So I and my companion set out, and the people were gathered around a group in the mosque. He said: So I made my way through them until I stood over them, and there were Ali ibn Abi Talib and al-Zubayr and Talhah and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas. He said: It was not quicker than Uthman coming walking, and he said: Is Ali here? They said: Yes. He said: Is al-Zubayr here? They said: Yes. He said: Is Talhah here? They said: Yes. He said: Is Sad here? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys the land of Banu so-and-so, Allah will forgive him? So I bought it, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought it. He said: Put it in our mosque and its reward is yours. They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys the well of Rumah? So I bought it for such-and-such, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought it, meaning the well of Rumah. He said: Make it a watering place for the Muslims and its reward is yours. They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, besides whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the faces of the people on the day of the Army of Hardship and said: Whoever equips these, Allah will forgive him? So I equipped them until they lacked neither bridle nor rope. They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. O Allah, bear witness. O Allah, bear witness. Then he left."
"512","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Sulayman ibn Atiq informed me from Abdullah ibn Babayah from one of the sons of Yala ibn Umayyah who said: Yala said: I performed tawaf with Uthman and we touched the Corner. Yala said: I was on the side toward the House, and when we reached the western Corner which is toward the Black, I pulled his hand for him to touch, so he said: What is the matter with you? I said: Will you not touch? He said: Did you not perform tawaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes indeed. He said: Did you see him touching these two western Corners? I said: No. He said: Is there not for you in him a good example? I said: Yes indeed. He said: Then pass on from you."
"513","Abu Abdurrahman al-Muqri narrated to us: Haywah narrated to us: Abu Aqil informed us that he heard al-Harith, freedman of Uthman, saying: Uthman sat one day and we sat with him, then the caller to prayer came to him, so he called for water in a vessel, I think it would contain a mudd, then he performed ablution, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution like this ablution of mine, then he said: And whoever performs ablution like my ablution, then stands and prays the noon prayer, he is forgiven what was between it and the dawn, then prays Asr, he is forgiven what is between it and the noon prayer, then prays Maghrib, he is forgiven what is between it and the Asr prayer, then prays Isha, he is forgiven what is between it and the Maghrib prayer, then perhaps he spends his night tossing, then if he stands and performs ablution and prays dawn, he is forgiven what is between it and the Isha prayer. And they are the good deeds that remove evil deeds. They said: These are the good deeds, so what are the lasting ones, O Uthman? He said: They are: There is no god but Allah, and Glory be to Allah, and Praise be to Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah."
"514","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As that Said ibn al-As informed him that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Uthman narrated to him that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on his bed wearing the cloak of Aishah, so he permitted Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was like that, so he fulfilled his need to him, then left. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission, so he permitted him while upon that state, so he fulfilled his need to him, then left. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Then I sought permission upon him, so he sat and said to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Gather your clothes upon you. So he fulfilled my need to me, then I left. Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O Messenger of Allah, why did I not see you show concern for Abu Bakr and Umar as you showed concern for Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uthman is a shy man, and I feared if I permitted him upon that state that he would not convey his need to me. And Layth said: And a group of people said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Shall I not feel shy from one whom the angels feel shy from."
"515","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Salih: Ibn Shihab said: Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As informed me that Said ibn al-As informed him that Uthman and Aishah narrated to him that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on his bed wearing the cloak of Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her. Then he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Uqayl."
"516","Yunus narrated to us: Layth narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, and Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Muadh ibn Abdurrahman al-Taymi, from Humran, freedman of Uthman, from Uthman ibn Affan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution and perfects ablution, then walks to a prescribed prayer and prays it, his sin is forgiven."
"517","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Abdurrahman ibn Mawhab, narrated to us: My uncle Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab informed me from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, went to Makkah as a pilgrim, and the wife of Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib came to him and he spent the night with her until morning, then he came in the morning with traces of perfume upon him and a saffron-dyed dyed cloak, and he caught up with the people at Malal before they set out. When Uthman saw him he rebuked him harshly and said: Do you wear dyed garments when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it? Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid him nor you, he only forbade me."
"518","Abdullah narrated to us: My father and Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, they said: Yaqub narrated to us: My father said in his hadith: The nephew of Ibn Shihab informed us, and Abu Khaythamah said: He narrated to me from his uncle who said: Salih ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah informed me that Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him that he heard Aban ibn Uthman saying: Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Consider, if there were a flowing river at the courtyard of one of you, he bathes from it five times every day, what would remain of his dirt? They said: Nothing. He said: The prayers remove sins as water removes dirt."
"519","Abu Abdurrahman said: I found in the book of my father: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Aswad narrated to me from Husayn ibn Umar from Makhariq ibn Abdullah ibn Jabir al-Ahmasi from Tariq ibn Shihab from Uthman ibn Affan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deceives the Arabs will not enter into my intercession, nor will my love reach him."
"520","Abdullah narrated to us: Abbas ibn Muhammad and Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz narrated to me, they said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from al-Awwam ibn Murajim of Banu Qays ibn Thalabah from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Uthman that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hornless will take retribution from the horned on the Day of Resurrection."
"521","Abdullah narrated to us: Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us: Al-Hasan narrated to us who said: I witnessed Uthman ordering in his sermon the killing of dogs and the slaughtering of pigeons."
"522","Abdullah narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Jarir narrated to us from al-Mughirah from Umm Musa who said: Uthman was among the most handsome of people."
"523","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us: My father narrated to me from his father who said: I was praying, then a man passed in front of me, so I prevented him but he refused. So I asked Uthman ibn Affan, and he said: It will not harm you, O son of my brother."
"524","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us: My father narrated to me from his father who said: Uthman said: If you find in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that you put my foot in fetters, then put it."
"525","Abdullah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Basri narrated to us: Al-Mughirah ibn Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us: My father Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Zayd ibn Ali ibn Husayn from his father Ali ibn Husayn from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah while having Usamah ibn Zayd riding behind him, and said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. Then he moved on traveling at a gentle pace, and the people began striking right and left, while he turned and said: Calmness, O people. Calmness, O people. Until he came to Muzdalifah and combined the two prayers. Then he stood at Muzdalifah and stood upon Quzah and took al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas riding behind him, and said: This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place. Then he moved on making gentle pace, and the people striking right and left, while he turned and said: Calmness, O people. Calmness. And he mentioned the hadith in full."
"526","Abdullah narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abi al-Yafur al-Abdi narrated to us from his father from Muslim Abu Said, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, that Uthman ibn Affan freed twenty slaves, and called for trousers and tightened them upon him, and he had not worn them in ignorance nor Islam, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) last night in a dream, and I saw Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and they said to me: Be patient, for you will break your fast with us tomorrow. Then he called for a copy of the Quran and spread it before him, then he was killed while it was before him."
"527","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Ata from Uthman who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution: He washed his face three times and his hands three times, and washed his forearms three times three times, and wiped his head, and washed his feet with washing."
"528","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to me: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us from Abu Mawdud from Muhammad ibn Kab from Aban ibn Uthman from Uthman that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing in the earth nor in the heaven harms, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing, three times, a sudden calamity will not surprise him until night, and whoever says it when he enters evening, a sudden calamity will not surprise him until morning, if Allah wills."
"529","Abdullah narrated to us: Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah from Aban ibn Uthman that he saw a funeral approaching, so when he saw it he stood, and said: I saw Uthman doing that, and he informed me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"530","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Ibn Abi Farwah from Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Morning sleep prevents provision."
"531","Abdullah narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me: Mahbub ibn Muhriz narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Farrukh from his father who said: I witnessed Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, buried in his clothes with his blood, and he was not washed."
"532","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Bazzaz Muhammad ibn Abdurrahim narrated to me: Al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm al-Kufi narrated to us: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us from Hisham ibn Ziyad al-Qurashi from his father from Mihjan, freedman of Uthman, from Uthman who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah shades a servant in His shade on a day when there is no shade except His shade: one who grants respite to a debtor in hardship, or waives for a debtor."
"533","Abdullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Uthman, meaning al-Harbi Abu Zakariya, narrated to me: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from a man he named from Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Morning sleep prevents provision."
"534","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Malik: Nafi narrated to me from Nubayh ibn Wahb from Aban ibn Uthman from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One in ihram does not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"535","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi: Nubayh ibn Wahb narrated to me who said: Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mamar sent me, and he was proposing the daughter of Shaybah ibn Uthman for his son, so he sent to Aban ibn Uthman while he was over the pilgrimage season, and said: Do I not see him as a bedouin? One in ihram does not marry nor give in marriage. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me of that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Nubayh narrated to me from his father likewise."
"536","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me: Zuhayr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Abdullah from Umm Hilal daughter of Waki from Nailah daughter of al-Farafisah, wife of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Commander of the Believers Uthman dozed and slumbered, then woke and said: The people will surely kill me. I said: No, if Allah wills, it will not reach that. Your subjects sought your redress. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in my dream, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and they said: You will break your fast with us tonight."
